Z||000000||d825077||05-05-2000||02:12 PM||||Last year my A/C worked great and was very cold.  Yesterday I tried it and it blew warm air.  Do you think my A/C system has a leak or just needs to be filled?  Is it hard to fill the A/C system?  Thank you.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||05-05-2000||02:18 PM||||If you're still running R12 there is nothing that you can do yourself you have to have it done by a pro.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-05-2000||02:21 PM||||unless the system was converted to R134a it is a federal crime to work on it yourself. (It's illegal in many countries now to work with R12.)<P>Likely the system has leaked off refrigerant. It needs to be serviced. This requires several tools. What tools depends on exactly what is wrong.<P>You cannot put R134 in an R12 system untill the system is completely pumped free of R12.<P>do a search. (Look in the archives section as well.) this has been repeatedly covered.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bad88||05-06-2000||12:32 AM||||Just a note .... I was shopping the blue light specials at K-mart last week and I noticed that they had a R-12 to 134a conversion kit for 60 bucks or so.  I didn't pay too much attention but it may be what you're lookig for.  Like I said I didn't look too close so I don't know if there is any special tools, parts legal stuff etc. but it cant hurt to check it out next time you're in K-Mart.||||reg||3
Z||000004||chris6878||05-06-2000||02:28 PM||||before i redid my v6 my air was very cold, i didnt disconnect any line, just dropped the complete thing from the engine and let it hang until it was re-assembled. <P>My air insnt cold now? but my belt is loose and squeels at times...    so i dunno..  it may have leaked off while i was redoing the engine..     could a loose belt cause the compressor not to work correctly (when i turn the air on sometimes the belt doesnt even turn)  too loose...   ||||reg||3
Z||000005||Old Lar||05-06-2000||08:34 PM||||Come on Chris - if the belt is loose and the compressor pully isn't turning, the A/C compressor isn't going to work and you won't get any cold air. Tighten the belt!<P>The belt may be shot if it has been squealing.  I've had that belt break.  Guess what I didn't have any A/C.||||reg||1
Z||000006||chris6878||05-06-2000||11:39 PM||||haha...  well.. i hope that the prob anyway...||||reg||3
Z||000007||d825077||05-09-2000||11:34 AM||||I had my system drained by a mechanic and bought the recharging kit at Kmart.  It was only $40.00 and worked great.  Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
